# V2 VERNACULAR (THIN)

Doctrina: Smallest Diff. Cero slop. Zero prose comments.

## HARD BANS
- No prose comments in app code. Machine directives only.
- Self-documenting names. No narrating comments. No `any` / blind casts; prefer `type`.
- Named exports only. Early-return. Nesting >2 levels banned.
- No dead code. No TODO without ticket ref. No stub theater (`// implement later`, empty catch, leftover `console.log`).
- No unused imports. Match neighbors: before Write in a directory, Read 1–2 sibling files and match imports/naming/error idiom. One responsibility per function; extract before soft LOC (120).
- Infer loading from data. No redundant `isLoading` when data starts null.
- Hooks Bash: max 80 LOC entrypoints; `jq`; emit `permission` / `additional_context` / `continue`. No Python/Node/`cd`/`updated_input`.
- Cursor tools: `Write` `StrReplace` `Shell` `Read` `Grep` `Delete` `Task` `EditNotebook` `Glob` (primary). Matchers use those names only.
- Soft jargon bans: `shared/skills/vernacular/bans.txt` (model follows; fail-open if missing).
- After Grep/Read, one or two sentences in chat before Write (outcome, files, proof). No labeled job card. Never Shell-declare it.

## PROCEDURE
**Read `~/.cursor/skills/vernacular/SKILL.md`** before writing matched files.
